# This root-level file is intentionally minimal — it previously duplicated
# (and had drifted out of sync with) the real environment variable names,
# which is a real risk in its own right: someone copying stale keys like
# JWT_SECRET/JWT_EXPIRES_IN here would get a boot-time validation error at
# best, or silently misconfigured auth at worst.
#
# The actual, up-to-date environment variables for each service live next
# to that service's code, since backend and frontend have separate .env
# files:
#
#   backend/.env.example
#   frontend/.env.example
#
# Copy each of those to backend/.env and frontend/.env respectively and
# fill in real values. NEVER commit .env or real secrets.
